<p>The main factor for code density is the possibility of returning inside the middle of an instruction bundle (dense vs aligned) and the using of nullification (null).
In common, code density for <archname/> is more or less similar to MIPS, PowerPC, Sparc, LoongArch, S390, and RISC-V (without compression) or only slightly worse.
This is surprising taking into account 128 registers, bundles, nops, etc.
The clear loser is MIPS.
</p>

